  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-PMR26-JOR101</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened policies and programmes on  women entrepreneurship, market systems, productivity,  access to finance, and the social and solidarity economy.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This outcome supports a more inclusive and competitive enterprise ecosystem in Jordan, with a focus on the social and solidarity economy (SSE) and export-oriented sectors. It addresses key constraints facing SMEs, including low productivity, limited access to finance, skills gaps, and weak market linkages.

The intervention strengthens the policy, legal, and institutional framework for SSE, particularly cooperatives, by advancing legislative reform, enhancing institutional capacities, and supporting implementation of the National Cooperative Strategy. It also promotes improved governance, digitization, inclusive finance, and sustainable business models, especially in agricultural value chains.

Expected results include stronger institutional frameworks for cooperatives, improved enterprise support services integrating competitiveness and decent work, and increased adoption of sustainable and inclusive business practices.

Beneficiaries include government institutions, employers&#x2019; and workers&#x2019; organizations, cooperatives, SMEs, and workers, particularly women and vulnerable groups. Implementation follows a tripartite, multi-stakeholder approach to ensure alignment with national priorities and sustainable results.</narrative>
  </description>
